{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_24e4648f94014fc28962dd80","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 151 lines\n1: Completed-GMT: 2026-10-11 07:11:26 GMT\n2: Completed-Local: 2026-10-11 14:11:26 Asia/Bangkok\n3: \n4: # semantic-register-vm phase 6, slice 6a\n5: \n6: Implementation is ready for non-author review. Acceptance items 1–10 pass on the executed lanes. Item 11's three-host gate is unmet: Dart is **NOT RUN**, blocked during compiler initialization by sandbox-denied Flutter cache writes. No review or sign-off is claimed; those remain assigned to claude-fable-5-1.\n7: \n8: Worktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6a`; branch: `srvm-phase6a`; HEAD remains `f11771e9`. No checkout switch, staging, or commit occurred. No governing design, phase-4b source, phase-5 source, or existing test was edited. No scanner, layout, `lift-task`, or `lower-task` was implemented.\n9: \n10: ## Changed files\n11: \n12: All four implementation/test files are **new**, currently untracked:\n13: \n14: | File | Work |\n15: |---|---|\n16: | `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` | Pure ordered `defect` and once-per-body `task-defect`; structural checks precede dependent reads; saved-window and lexical/free-environment checks; contexts and tail bookkeeping. |\n17: | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` | Declarative row/pending tables, frame bijection, content addresses, census, refinement and exhaustive individualization search, child cell scopes, bounded work, graph decoding, numbering before frame checks, and correspondence-based re-emission. |\n18: | `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc` | Evaluator-minted reference frames, four wrapper shapes, empty-K root tail call, twenty-five tamper rows, nil membership, free-env shadowing, structural precedence, integral float carrier refusal, and tail bookkeeping. |\n19: | `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc` | Bijection including full nested capture/closure structure, hashes, window canonicality, cell/stream renaming, unordered store containers, alias topology, census authentication, bounded search, child scopes/DAG sharing, full pending-envelope preservation, and task-root validation order. |\n20: \n21: Modified tracked files: **none**. New supporting artifacts under `collab/` include this report, lane logs, nine mutation logs, `6a-mutations.py`, `6a-mutations.json`, and the verified source backups. The pre-existing task prompt/stdout files were present before work; they are not claimed as authored deliverables.\n22: \n23: ## Exact verification outcomes\n24: \n25: | Lane/check | Outcome | Tests | Assertions | Failures | Errors | Evidence |\n26: |---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n27: | G0, final frame namespace | PASS, exit 0 | 9 | 221 | 0 | 0 | `collab/6a-frame-g0-final.log` |\n28: | G0, final rows namespace | PASS, exit 0 | 12 | 260 | 0 | 0 | `collab/6a-rows-g0-final.log` |\n29: | JVM, selected 14 namespaces | PASS, exit 0 | 186 | 4701 | 0 | 0 | `collab/6a-jvm-final.log` |\n30: | JVM, Node's additional parity dependency | PASS, exit 0 | 5 | 60 | 0 | 0 | `collab/6a-jvm-dependency-parity.log` |\n31: | Node, selected namespaces plus required parity dependency | PASS, exit 0 | 191 | 4760 | 0 | 0 | `collab/6a-node-final.log` |\n32: | Dart attempt | **NOT RUN**; compile command exit 1 | — | — | — | — | `collab/6a-dart.log` |\n33: | kondo, four changed paths | PASS, exit 0; 0 errors, 0 warnings | — | — | — | — | `collab/6a-kondo-final.log` |\n34: | cljstyle, four changed paths | PASS, exit 0 | — | — | — | — | `collab/6a-cljstyle-final.log`, final direct check |\n35: | trailing whitespace, four changed paths | PASS; zero matches; `rg` exit 1 means no matches | — | — | — | — | `collab/6a-whitespace-final.log`, final direct scan |\n36: \n37: Node additionally lists `Testing yin.vm.parity-test`, brought in by test dependencies. It also explicitly lists `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test` and `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`. Its build finished with zero warnings. The JVM-only source-purity assertion accounts for one assertion absent on Node; the parity dependency was run separately on JVM so its outcome is explicit.\n38: \n39: Exact final G0 commands:\n40: \n41: ```sh\n42: clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test\n43: clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test\n44: ```\n45: \n46: Exact selected JVM command:\n47: \n48: ```sh\n49: clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.code-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.vm-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.effects-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.parity-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.link-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.load-paths-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.walker-trace-test -n yin.vm.ucf-test -n yin.vm.ucf.handoff-test -n yin.vm.ucf.safepoint-harness-test\n50: clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.parity-test\n51: ```\n52: \n53: Exact Node command (foreground, via the `:cljs` alias):\n54: \n55: ```sh\n56: clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge '{:ns-regexp \"^(yin\\\\.vm\\\\.semantic-register\\\\..*-test|yin\\\\.vm\\\\.ucf\\\\.(rows|handoff|safepoint-harness)-test|yin\\\\.vm\\\\.ucf-test)$\"}'\n57: ```\n58: \n59: Exact Dart attempt:\n60: \n61: ```sh\n62: bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test,yin.vm.ucf.rows-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.code-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.vm-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.effects-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.parity-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.link-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.load-paths-test,yin.vm.semantic-register.walker-trace-test,yin.vm.ucf-test,yin.vm.ucf.handoff-test,yin.vm.ucf.safepoint-harness-test\n63: ```\n64: \n65: The Dart attempt produced these actual errors, before tests could execute:\n66: \n67: ```text\n68: /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/flutter/3.47.6-stable/bin/internal/update_engine_version.sh: line 71: /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/flutter/3.47.6-stable/bin/cache/engine.stamp.tmp.56585: Operation not permitted\n69: /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/flutter/3.47.6-stable/bin/internal/update_engine_version.sh: line 78: /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/flutter/3.47.6-stable/bin/cache/engine.realm: Operation not permitted\n70: Execution error at cljd.compiler/mk-live-analyzer-info (compiler.cljc:214).\n71: EOF while reading\n72: Exception in thread \"Thread-0\" java.lang.RuntimeException: Operation not permitted (sysctl failed)\n73: cljd compile failed, exit 1\n74: ```\n75: \n76: The log includes repeated denied cache writes with other PID suffixes. No Dart compile/test success or Dart assertion count is claimed. No sandbox escalation was requested. The orchestrator must re-run the lanes.\n77: \n78: Exact lint/format/whitespace commands:\n79: \n80: ```sh\n81: clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc\n82: cljstyle check src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc\n83: rg -n '[[:blank:]]+$' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc test/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame_test.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc\n84: ```\n85: \n86: No full `bb test` or full `bb test:sub yin.vm` run occurred. The task's explicit scoped lane instructions were followed, with every `-n` written literally; no shell word-splitting variable or background execution was used.\n87: \n88: ## Numbered acceptance list (§8.1)\n89: \n90: 1. **PASS — `contract-is-pure`.** Public `defect` takes `[frame code-map context task]`. It reads plain task data and no running kernel or engine. The JVM test inspects the namespace form for forbidden engine/kernel dependencies; its reader conditional puts `:cljd` first.\n91: 2. **PASS on JVM/Node — `every-reference-frame-validates`.** Forty-nine runs: rows 1, 2, 5, 6, 13–16, 18, 19, 21, 22 across bare/operand/depth-3/captured wrappers, plus row 20 unwrapped. Waits, parked records, each K through its enclosing frame, and recursively reached captures validate. Row 18 carries a composition-created module-store snapshot with two cursors and a module-owned closure. Row 19 is checked as halted, with no invented frame. Row 20 asserts empty K. Fixture setup distinctions are recorded below.\n92: 3. **PASS — `each-rule-refuses-its-tamper` and `first-defect-is-structural`.** The table has 24 frame tamper rows (C2 contributes kind and bounds), plus X1 through `task-defect`, giving the prescribed 25 rows for 24 rules. Each frame result checks the expected kind and a vector path. Malformed K beats the bad window. Additional integral-float, delivery, bookkeeping, and nil-presence checks supplement the table.\n93: 4. **PASS — `nil-valued-register-is-a-member`.** An actual row-22 saved window has a present nil-valued key; deleting it yields `:window-missing`. The codec bijection retains the key as `[:lit nil]`.\n94: 5. **PASS — `worked-example-saved`.** `saved(4,2) = #{1}` is asserted against computed liveness. The valid `{1 :f}`, self `{1 :f 2 :x}`, missing `{}`, and extra `{1 :f 3 :x}` cases give the specified outcomes.\n95: 6. **PASS — `free-env-mismatch`.** Row 21 starts with `{x 99 y 7}`, and its parked activation binds lexical x to 1. Changing/removing unshadowed y fails, removing lexical x fails, changing lexical x to 98 passes, and reserved `yin/def` in the root environment fails X1.\n96: 7. **PASS — `bijection`.** Every reference fixture's frame is classified into portable codec values and round-trips exactly. Closures retain segment address, entry, params, lexical environment and store-of; captures retain full act/K structure, including nested captures. Native seals and host objects are classified by test helpers, not treated as portable literals. The converse re-emission retains the root id.\n97: 8. **PASS — `row-ids-are-jing-default`.** Every emitted content row equals `jing/segment-key` of its body and parses as algorithm `:blake3`. No legacy body reader or alternate identity scheme was added.\n98: 9. **PASS — `window-sorted-and-unique`.** Rehashed out-of-order and duplicate-key window tampers refuse as `:yin.k/undecodable` in canonical form; they are not merely hash mismatches or later frame refusals.\n99: 10. **PASS — `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`.** Distinct lane stream identities/source cell identities, explicitly permuted wire cell numbering, and a store payload containing a stream set and a cursor-keyed map re-emit to equal roots under explicit correspondence maps. Missing correspondence coverage fails. Alias topology, authenticated cell positions, symmetric search/multiplicity, work exhaustion, and child scopes are separately tested.\n100: 11. **FAIL / gate unmet — three-host verification.** Kondo is clean and the selected JVM/Node suites pass, with both required new namespaces printed on Node. Dart is NOT RUN because of the recorded sandbox block. A three-host green claim and sign-off would be false.\n101: \n102: ## Tests that can fail: actual source mutations\n103: \n104: Backups were taken **before any mutation** into `collab/6a-verified-backups/`, and verified with `cmp`. The final source remains byte-identical to those backups:\n105: \n106: ```text\n107: frame.cljc SHA-256 30cfb19446e8311b3d15c9f739e22d899ff918835df21f7092c89dc31c4b4ca0\n108: rows.cljc  SHA-256 50560bddf8227efdb6c37eb55d8a845fc6de167c619cfbf7e3538fc46c98e2a6\n109: ```\n110: \n111: These SHA-256 values are backup integrity checks, not code/row identities; all new code/row identities use Jing's default digest.\n112: \n113: Every mutant was applied to one source file, run in the foreground, and restored from its verified backup in a `finally` block. After **each** restoration, `cmp <path> <backup>` and `git diff --quiet HEAD -- <path>` both exited 0. Since these are new untracked source files, the HEAD diff alone is not proof of restoration; the byte comparison and SHA checks provide that proof. No mutation survived.\n114: \n115: | ID | Temporary source mutation | Named test with actual FAIL | Assertions | Failures/errors | Exit | Restore cmp / HEAD diff |\n116: |---|---|---|---:|---|---:|---|\n117: | M1 | Disable missing saved-window membership check | `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member` | 3 | 1 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n118: | M2 | Disable required lexical-key presence | `frame-test/free-env-mismatch` | 7 | 1 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n119: | M3 | Disable equality outside the lexical chain | `frame-test/free-env-mismatch` | 7 | 2 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n120: | M4 | Bypass destination equality | `frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper` | 50 | 1 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n121: | M5 | Use L(pc) instead of saved(pc,rd), retaining the virtual destination | `frame-test/worked-example-saved` | 5 | 1 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n122: | M6 | Suppress the cross-body resume-pc defect | `frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper` | 50 | 1 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n123: | M7 | Suppress canonical-numbering root comparison | `rows-test/numbering-precedes-frame-defect` | 2 | 1 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n124: | M8 | Bypass required stream-correspondence coverage | `rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant` | 3 | 1 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n125: | M9 | Remove the search-node budget charge | `rows-test/refinement-search-preserves-unordered-multiplicity` | 4 | 2 / 0 | 1 | 0 / 0 |\n126: \n127: Each ran exactly one named test using:\n128: \n129: ```sh\n130: clojure -M:test -n <literal namespace> -v <fully qualified literal test var>\n131: ```\n132: \n133: The exact argv, logs, exit codes, named-failure checks and restoration results are in `collab/6a-mutations.json`; the reproducible foreground runner is `collab/6a-mutations.py`; each test's actual FAIL output is in `collab/6a-M1.log` through `collab/6a-M9.log`. Test fixtures were subsequently strengthened with the explicit wire-number permutation/store payload and a full task-root check; the mutated production source itself was not subsequently changed.\n134: \n135: ## Ambiguities, findings, and smallest readings\n136: \n137: - **Unspecified codec API details (§2.7/§8.1).** The design names the frame bijection and abstract-task procedure without concrete function signatures for their auxiliary representation. The implementation documents `{:kind k :slots [...]}` abstract rows, explicit decoded row/cell wrappers, and optional value encoder/decoder arguments. `frame->rows` returns a frame-rooted codec fragment in the version-3 envelope; `emit` accepts an already assembled abstract task. These are codec operations, not an exported running task or `lift-task`/`lower-task`. The full transport path still belongs to 6b.\n138: - **Purity dependency list (§3.1).** E2 needs the set of names over A's lexical owner chain, rather than a positional name lookup. The validator directly walks `code/body-ranges` and closure params, so `debruijn/resolve-name` is unnecessary and is not required. This preserves the specified chain/presence semantics, including shadowing and duplicate names, while avoiding an unused dependency.\n139: - **Resource refusal spelling (§8 diagnostics versus draft §10.10).** §10.10 expressly leaves work-bound limits and refusal mapping to implementation/composition and calls for a qualified unsupported/resource refusal. The codec uses `:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported`, kind `:resource-limit`, and a budget-category path. It never returns `:noncanonical-cells` for unfinished search and never attaches a resource. This specific spelling merits reviewer confirmation against the draft's general “no new top-level outcome” wording; no design was amended. Defaults are 10,000 rows, 64 cells, depth 256, 200,000 work charges, 10,000 search nodes and 16,777,216 encoded bytes; callers may tighten/override bounds without changing canonical bytes.\n140: - **Reference fixture setup (§5.2 versus 6a's frame-only acceptance).** Streams/cursors are supplied by the test composition. Row 20 uses a preconstructed cursor stored under c and executes the same unwrapped root tail-call body, instead of replaying the design's two-batch setup; the test asserts empty K and the resulting minted tail frame. Row 18 mirrors the existing composition-created module-store snapshot shape using the register machine. These tests establish validator/codec facts, not full task transport or post-lower execution. The latter belongs to 6b.\n141: - **Initial fixture errors were real failures, not implementation evidence.** Early iterations had reader errors, an unresolved `stream/next!` caused by a missing stream-module registry, and a numbering tamper that was out of order and correctly failed at the earlier canonical-form gate. Those were corrected. A preliminary frame-namespace invocation made before its test file existed ran zero tests and is not counted as a passing G0 check. An earlier native-value projection omitted closure/capture internals; the final bijection classifies and retains their complete portable structure instead.\n142: - **Numbers were checked, not silently corrected.** The initial analysis baseline `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis-test` passed 8 tests/497 assertions, including the worked liveness facts. The new tamper-table count (24 frame rows plus X1) and `saved(4,2)=#{1}` passed on their first executable checks. The earliest whole-matrix attempt threw during fixture construction before reaching its 49-run count assertion; that count was established after fixing the fixture, and is not claimed as verified in that failed attempt. No wrong hand-derived saved-register or oracle number was found.\n143: - **Clock discrepancy.** The completion timestamp is the clock tool's actual `2026-10-11 07:11:26 UTC`, converted to Bangkok. It precedes the supplied Created-GMT 07:30 marker; that supplied marker was not used to invent a later completion time.\n144: \n145: ## Unresolved concerns and incomplete work\n146: \n147: - Dart compilation and execution remain unverified. The orchestrator must run the scoped Dart lane, and re-run all lanes before acceptance.\n148: - Non-author review/sign-off remains outstanding. In particular, review the concrete resource-refusal spelling and the documented codec-fragment API boundary.\n149: - The codec consumes classified portable values/abstract rows. It does not authenticate native seals, scan dependencies/trees, serve or attach streams, enforce custody admission, reconstruct a kernel, or perform full task lift/lower. Those are intentionally outside 6a and no end-to-end task-transport success is claimed.\n150: - Full task transport (6b) and layouts (6c) remain unimplemented by this slice, as required.\n151: - The implementation and executed checks are complete for the claimed scope; the three-host acceptance gate is incomplete. Nothing was staged or committed."}],"deferred":false}}
{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_14f526446f8d4732aa40022b","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 124 lines\n1: Completed-GMT: 2026-10-11 09:05:00 GMT\n2: Completed-Local: 2026-10-11 16:05:00 Asia/Bangkok\n3: \n4: # Adversarial review of slice 6a (register frame validator and row codec)\n5: \n6: Reviewer: claude-fable-5-1 (non-author family). Author: codex gpt-6.1-sol.\n7: Worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6a`, branch `srvm-phase6a`, HEAD 4b0e735e, diff `master...HEAD` = exactly the four new files (frame.cljc 162 lines, rows.cljc 677, frame_test.cljc 281, rows_test.cljc 247). Nothing staged or committed by me; `git diff --quiet HEAD -- src/` exits 0 at the end of the review and both sources `cmp` equal to `collab/6a-reviewer-backups/{frame,rows}.cljc`.\n8: \n9: ## What I ran (all foreground, all in this worktree)\n10: \n11: | Lane / check | Command | Outcome |\n12: |---|---|---|\n13: | JVM baseline | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test` | 21 tests, 481 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n14: | **Dart** (nobody had run it) | `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test,yin.vm.ucf.rows-test` | compile OK; **21 tests: 20 passed, 1 FAILED** (`yin.vm.ucf.rows-test/task-root-checks-carried-code-and-frame`); log `collab/6a-reviewer-dart.log` |\n15: | Node | not re-run by me; the author's `collab/6a-node-final.log` shows `Testing yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test` and `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`, 191 tests / 4760 assertions / 0 failures |\n16: | Mutation campaign | `python3 -I collab/6a-reviewer-mutants.py` (44 mutants + 1 rerun), each `clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>` with literal names | 29 KILLED, 15 SURVIVED; per-mutant logs `collab/6a-reviewer-R*.log`, table `collab/6a-reviewer-mutants-main.json` (+ `6a-reviewer-mutants.json` for the R23 rerun) |\n17: | Derivation probe | temporary print-probe appended to rows.cljc (`collab/6a-reviewer-probe.cljc`), run through `rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default`, restored | output `collab/6a-reviewer-P00.log` (80 `RVPROBE` lines) |\n18: \n19: Backups and restoration: my backups live in `collab/6a-reviewer-backups/`; the harness refuses to mutate unless each backup `cmp`-equals its source and the source is clean against HEAD, and after every mutant it restores from the backup and records `cmp` and `git diff --quiet HEAD -- <path>` (both 0 for all 45 runs). **Process incident, reported plainly:** my very first harness run applied the probe to rows.cljc before any reviewer backup existed (my earlier backup command had been refused by the sandbox as a whole, which I missed), and the harness crashed before restoring. I restored rows.cljc from the author's verified backup `collab/6a-verified-backups/rows.cljc` (`cmp` 0, `git diff --quiet HEAD -- src/` 0) before doing anything else; the guard above was added afterwards. The probe's output from that run is the one used below.\n20: \n21: The sandbox refused every non-`clojure -M:test` way of evaluating project code (`clojure -Sdeps`, `clojure -M:cljs -i`, `java -cp`), so the \"independent derivations\" were done by hand on paper and compared against values printed by the probe; the probe computed Merkle ids for row sets I constructed by hand from the design tables, using only `jing/segment-key`.\n22: \n23: ## Findings (severity | file:line | evidence | correction)\n24: \n25: 1. **HIGH | test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:238 | Dart lane fails.** `task-root-checks-carried-code-and-frame` throws `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/kind :extra-cell :yin.k/path [9]}` on Dart only. Cause: `(assoc (:slots base) 2 :blocked 11 ft/worked-code 13 [wait] 16 {...})` is a multi-key `assoc` on a **vector**; ClojureDart inlines it to `(-conj v {2 … 11 … 13 … 16 …})`, which appends the map as an 18th slot and leaves slot 13 (frames) empty, so the census cell `:test/cursor` is never reached (generated `test/cljd-out/yin/vm/ucf/rows-test_test.dart:4820-4835` shows the `PersistentHashMap` being `-conj`ed). The same trap is recorded in memory for nil; it applies to vectors too. Correction: chain single-key assocs (`(-> slots (assoc 2 :blocked) (assoc 11 ft/worked-code) (assoc 13 [wait]) (assoc 16 {...}))`). Production code is free of this (frame_test.cljc:120 and :273 multi-key assocs are on maps; rows.cljc has none). Acceptance item 11 therefore FAILS on Dart with a concrete failure, not just \"NOT RUN\".\n26: \n27: 2. **MEDIUM | src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:119 | malformed census key escapes as a host exception.** `ordered-slots :cells` sorts by `(edn/read-string (subs (name k) 2))`; this runs at decode step 5 (`:row-order`, line 473) on wire data before numbering. Probe: a `:cells` row keyed `:x` (rehashed consistently) gives `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException`, not `:yin.k/undecodable`. `emit-numbered` with a partial numbering fails the same way. Correction: validate `:C` slots of the census against `#\"c-[1-9][0-9]*\"` in `structural?` (refuse `:slot-kind`), and parse digits with a guard instead of the EDN reader.\n28: \n29: 3. **MEDIUM | src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:424 | gate reads an unvalidated slot.** `gate` does `(doseq [install (nth slots 12)] …)` before the schema step checked slot kinds. Probe: installs slot `5` → `IllegalArgumentException: Don't know how to create ISeq from: java.lang.Long`. (The frames slot set to `5` is correctly refused `:slot-kind`.) Correction: in `gate`, require `(and (vector? installs) (every? keyword? installs))`, refusing `:task-shape`.\n30: \n31: 4. **MEDIUM | test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:143-156 | acceptance item 10's \"unordered-container permutation\" is vacuous.** Mutant R26 (emit `:set` slots unsorted) SURVIVES the whole suite. Fixture `b` swaps the stream *identities* and the correspondence map \"accordingly\", so after substitution the set's elements are in the **same abstract order** as in `a`; the cursor-keyed map is resolved by refinement (`'one → x`), so its order is identical too. `refinement-search-preserves-unordered-multiplicity` cannot see it either: when every element is a cell, the exhaustive search picks the bytewise-min leaf and so compensates for an unsorted set. Correction: emit one task whose `:set`/`:map` slots are listed in reversed abstract order under the **identity** correspondence and assert equal roots (streams, not only cells, in the set).\n32: \n33: 5. **MEDIUM | test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc | the canonical procedure's specific output is unpinned.** Mutants R21 (number classes n…1 instead of 1…n) and R17 (search keeps the first explored leaf instead of the bytewise-min) SURVIVE. No test pins a root id, and no fixture leaves a non-automorphic class after refinement (the draft §6 triangle/square case), so an implementation that is deterministic but disagrees with the design's procedure (or depends on hash-map traversal order in `search`) passes. Correction: pin at least one root id (probe values: fixture `(fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y)` → `:segment/blake3-be82d50b14804bb7a69103631b9c45759b49b67dbb3cebe75a1259fed6b4a937`; `(frame->rows ft/worked-frame)` → `:segment/blake3-c4a7c7e6de3b44400efec5930bc3d85d86b29153b4b2d548acba630bfbc3da7d`) and add a fixture with two refinement-equivalent but non-automorphic cells whose chosen leaf is asserted.\n34: \n35: 6. **MEDIUM (6b boundary, decide now) | src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:534-536, 541-544 | in-band value markers.** The default `value-node`/`decoded-value` use plain maps `{:yin.k/row n}`/`{:yin.k/cell id}` as markers, so a *guest* map with exactly that key is misread. Probe: window value `{:yin.k/row 1}` round-trips to a `:row-shape` refusal; a map-shaped payload would be silently reinterpreted. §2.7's bijection does not hold on such frames. 6b's lift supplies its own classifier, but the default codec path (and `rows->frame`) should either use a distinct marker type (record/`deftype`) or refuse those maps as `:yin.k/non-portable`.\n36: \n37: 7. **LOW | src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc:32 + rows.cljc:552-554, 604-608 | `store-of nil` breaks the identity.** A keyed frame with `:yin.k/store-of nil` present passes S4 (`closed?` allows the optional key with any value) but encodes to `[:env b nil]` and decodes without the key: `frame->rows ∘ rows->frame ≠ id` (probe: `false`). Correction: S4 refuses a present nil `store-of` (`:env-shape`), or the design states canonical frames omit it.\n38: \n39: 8. **LOW | rows.cljc:119 vs draft §3/§5 | census ordering ambiguity not recorded by the author.** Draft §3 says the census is \"sorted by n\"; draft §5's \"one ordering rule\" says sorted by canonical bytes of the key as spelled. They differ from ten cells on (`c-10` sorts before `c-2` bytewise). The implementation follows §3 (probe: ten cells emit `c-1 … c-10` numerically and decode). Record the reading; the suite has no ≥10-cell case.\n40: \n41: 9. **LOW | rows.cljc:393 | step-5 literal rules skipped for frame-rooted packs.** `check-abstract!` runs only for `:task` roots, so `rows->frame` accepts a `:vec` row of pure literals or a non-portable `[:lit obj]`. Acceptable for a test device; note it so 6b never routes a frame-rooted pack to `rows->frame` as a trust boundary.\n42: \n43: 10. **LOW | rows.cljc:151 vs 210 | child budget.** `emit-node` numbers an install child with `(canonical-numbering x)` (default budget) while `ce` passes the caller's `budget`; a tightened `:search`/`:work` bound does not reach children on emit.\n44: \n45: 11. **LOW | rows.cljc:656-658, 674-676 | defect path vocabulary.** Frame defects are reported as `[root-id :frames i …keyed-path]`, not the draft §8's `[row-id slot-index …]`. Harmless, but two path dialects now exist in one refusal family.\n46: \n47: 12. **LOW | test gaps shown by surviving mutants** (none is a code defect; the probe confirmed the code refuses correctly where it could be checked): R06 non-vector `:yin.k/k` (code gives `:k-shape`), R07 `pc 0` (code gives `:pc-bounds`), R10 A5-before-A6 order (code gives `:window-extra` for `{3 :x}`), R12 P2's empty admit set for `:park`/`:current-continuation`, R24 extra top-level wire key (code refuses `:row-shape`), R25 X1-before-frames order, R29 gate cycle check (redundant with `walk`), R30 malformed carried code (`:code`), R33 non-portable `[:lit …]` (`:literal`), R35 decoded-equality duplicate keys, R45 `:yin.k/hash-mismatch` (a stale id is still caught later as `:noncanonical-cells`, but the step-4 kind is never asserted), R46 `:reference-kind`. Each needs one assertion.\n48: \n49: 13. **INFO | honesty of claims.** (a) The author's report is honest about Dart (NOT RUN) and about the resource-refusal spelling and the `debruijn/resolve-name` deviation; my hand derivation of row 21's chain agrees with `lexical-names` (`#{x f cat}`), so the deviation is sound. (b) Acceptance item 2 says the task context is \"decoded from the machine's own tables\"; the test takes `:free-env` from the fixture's setup `env` and a constant `:ffi-call-ids #{}` (frame_test.cljc:20, 124). Accurate for stage-1 rows (no FFI), but not what the sentence says. (c) `refinement-search-preserves-unordered-multiplicity` does not exercise duplicate multiplicity; the name overclaims. (d) `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant` tests identity renaming, not container permutation (finding 4). (e) The author did not record the census-ordering ambiguity (finding 8) or the marker ambiguity (finding 6).\n50: \n51: ## Answers to the six questions\n52: \n53: **1. Can each acceptance item's test fail?** Yes for items 1-9 (named killing mutants in the table): item 3's `each-rule-refuses-its-tamper` killed 12 rule mutants (R08, R11, R13, R14, R37-R44) and `first-defect-is-structural` killed the S2/S3 reorder (R02); item 4 killed R01 and R31; item 5 killed R09; item 6 killed R03 and R04; item 7 killed R19 and R31; item 8 killed R15 and R23; item 9 killed R27. Item 10: only R36 (missing correspondence) is killed; R17, R21 and R26 survive, so its permutation and canonicality clauses are not actually tested (findings 4, 5). Item 11 FAILS on Dart (finding 1). The author's nine mutants all map onto killed mutants of mine (M1≈R01/R31, M2≈R03, M4≈R13, M6≈R08, M7≈R28, M8≈R36, M9≈R32); M3 and M5 I did not replicate.\n54: \n55: **2. Rule coverage.** The tamper table has 24 frame rows plus X1 through `task-defect` = 25, each refused with its own kind (T1 and A1 legitimately share `:site`, A2/T1 share `:deliver`, as the design names them). The published input contract is plain data `{:free-env :parked-key :ffi-call-ids}` (frame.cljc:61-65). The `ns` form requires `yin.vm`, `.code`, `.analysis` only; no kernel, no `yin.vm.engine` (`yin.vm` is permitted by §3.1 and transitively loads dao.stream/dao.space.query, not the engine). Design order S→C→A/T→K→E→P is implemented; the only ordering mutant tried (R02) was killed.\n56: \n57: **3. Row codec.** Bijection holds on all 49 fixtures' frames (bijection test + R19/R31 killed) with classified values and a substituted pending; the evaluator's real pending fields are 6b's. Hand Merkle re-derivation of row 22's frame equals the codec root (below). Numbering: I reviewed `ce`, `positions`, `refine`, `search` against draft §6 steps 1-5 and found no encounter-order dependence (class order by label bytes, positions sorted, leaf chosen by min root body bytes; `ids` order only affects which automorphic cell gets which number, unobservable in the rows); renaming invariance confirmed by the probe (`{:x c-1 :y c-2}` vs `{:y c-1 :x c-2}` with equal roots). BLAKE3 only: no `sha` in either source; R23 (sha256) killed by the algorithm assertion. §5.5 re-emission is correspondence-based (R36 killed) but the permutation test is vacuous (finding 4). The exhaustive search's min-selection is untested (finding 5).\n58: \n59: **4. Independent derivations.** (a) Worked example `[:var 1 f] [:var 3 g] [:var 4 x] [:call 2 3 [4] false] [:var 5 y] [:call 0 1 [2 5] false] [:halt 0]`: L(5) = {1 2 5}, L(4) = use(4) ∪ (L(5) − def(4)) = {1 2}, saved(4,2) = {1}; matches the test and `analysis_test`. (b) Row 22 bare: act at pc 8 after `[:stream-next 3 4]`, rd 3, body registers 5, window keys {1 (the `cat` closure), 2 (the nil operand p)}, saved = {1 2}; design form `[:window 1 V 2 [:lit nil]]`. With opaque values I hand-built every row from the §2.3 tables (`:bindings` sorted by key bytes, `:env [bindings nil]`, `:window`, `:kframe [A pc env window rd]`, `:k`, `:act [A pc env window k rd]`, `:pending [:next :test/cursor]`, `:wait [act pending]`), hashed each with `jing/segment-key`, and got root `:segment/blake3-8c14cb536dd98a1c62cd00c3b577f11c23ed936d0d599186857d43fa3fb329d2` = the codec's root; the hand window row `[:window 1 [:lit :v] 2 [:lit nil]]` has id `…169e5b7a…` present in the wire, and the kframe's empty window is `[:window]` as §2.3 requires. (c) Row 21: body-ranges owners 13→`[x]`, 4→`[f]`, 0→`[cat]`, so C = {x f cat}; E = {cat f x 1 y 7}, free-env {x 99 y 7}; off C both are {y 7}; matches `lexical-names`. The tests pin no hash values (finding 5), so these were compared structurally and via the probe's ids.\n60: \n61: **5. Scope and portability.** Only the four new files changed; nothing of 4b/5 touched. No `#'` in sources or tests. Reader conditionals are `:cljd`-first. No `for`. Nil-valued keys preserved (R19/R31 killed). The one portability defect is the multi-key vector `assoc` (finding 1). `clojure.edn` is available on cljd (used elsewhere), but its use on wire data is finding 2.\n62: \n63: **6. Honest claims.** See finding 13. Nothing in the author's report claims a run that did not occur; my Dart run shows the sandbox block was environmental.\n64: \n65: ## Mutant table\n66: \n67: | ID | File | Mutation | Named test | Result |\n68: |---|---|---|---|---|\n69: | R01 | frame | A6 `window-missing` dropped | frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member | KILLED (1/3 assertions, :208) |\n70: | R02 | frame | S2 and S3 reordered (window before K) | frame-test/first-defect-is-structural | KILLED (:224) |\n71: | R03 | frame | E2 lexical presence not required | frame-test/free-env-mismatch | KILLED (:218) |\n72: | R04 | frame | X1 reserved names unchecked | frame-test/free-env-mismatch | KILLED (:220) |\n73: | R05 | frame | P4 bookkeeping key membership dropped | frame-test/tail-bookkeeping-and-delivery | KILLED (:274) |\n74: | R06 | frame | S2 non-vector K accepted | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | SURVIVED |\n75: | R07 | frame | C2 `pc > 0` bound dropped | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | SURVIVED |\n76: | R08 | frame | C3 pc-body unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n77: | R09 | frame | A4 `window-self` dropped | frame-test/worked-example-saved | KILLED (:197) |\n78: | R10 | frame | A5/A6 order swapped | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | SURVIVED |\n79: | R11 | frame | E1 reserved binding unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n80: | R12 | frame | P2: `:park`/`:current-continuation` admit `:next` | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | SURVIVED |\n81: | R13 | frame | A2 destination equality dropped | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n82: | R14 | frame | K1 return-site unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n83: | R15 | rows | row id hashed without its first child slot | rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default | KILLED (10 failures) |\n84: | R16 | rows | census extra cell not refused | rows-test/schema-and-literal-canonicality | KILLED (:202) |\n85: | R17 | rows | search keeps first explored leaf (input-order tie break) | rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant | SURVIVED |\n86: | R19 | rows | window nil-valued key dropped on encode | rows-test/bijection | KILLED (4 failures) |\n87: | R21 | rows | numbering reversed (cells swapped) | rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant | SURVIVED |\n88: | R22 | rows | `:rows` budget charge removed | rows-test/schema-and-literal-canonicality | KILLED (:208) |\n89: | R23 | rows | digest changed to sha256 (`{:algorithm :sha256}`; first attempt with a bare keyword was a no-op and is discounted) | rows-test/row-ids-are-jing-default | KILLED (26 failures) |\n90: | R24 | rows | extra top-level wire key accepted | rows-test/gates-and-graph-before-hashes | SURVIVED |\n91: | R25 | rows | X1 judged after waits | rows-test/numbering-precedes-frame-defect | SURVIVED |\n92: | R26 | rows | `:set` slots not sorted on emit | rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant | SURVIVED |\n93: | R27 | rows | row-order check removed | rows-test/window-sorted-and-unique | KILLED (:140) |\n94: | R28 | rows | `:noncanonical-cells` comparison removed | rows-test/numbering-precedes-frame-defect | KILLED (:195) |\n95: | R29 | rows | gate cycle check removed | rows-test/child-scope-and-shared-child-dag | SURVIVED |\n96: | R30 | rows | carried code well-formedness unchecked | rows-test/task-root-checks-carried-code-and-frame | SURVIVED |\n97: | R31 | rows | `[:lit nil]` decoded as absence | rows-test/bijection | KILLED (8 failures) |\n98: | R32 | rows | search bound removed | rows-test/refinement-search-preserves-unordered-multiplicity | KILLED (2 failures) |\n99: | R33 | rows | non-portable literal accepted | rows-test/schema-and-literal-canonicality | SURVIVED |\n100: | R34 | rows | reference-free collection row accepted | rows-test/schema-and-literal-canonicality | KILLED (:203) |\n101: | R35 | rows | decoded-equality duplicate key unchecked | rows-test/schema-and-literal-canonicality | SURVIVED |\n102: | R36 | rows | missing stream correspondence guessed | rows-test/canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant | KILLED (:155) |\n103: | R37 | frame | P3 captured-site unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED (2) |\n104: | R38 | frame | P1 pending presence unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n105: | R39 | frame | T1 tail site unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n106: | R40 | frame | S1 closed key set unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED (2) |\n107: | R41 | frame | K3 return window unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED (2) |\n108: | R42 | frame | K2 return destination unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n109: | R43 | frame | C1 segment membership unchecked | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n110: | R44 | frame | S3 window keys not required to be registers | frame-test/each-rule-refuses-its-tamper | KILLED |\n111: | R45 | rows | row hash equality unchecked on decode | rows-test/window-sorted-and-unique | SURVIVED |\n112: | R46 | rows | structural reference kind unchecked | rows-test/schema-and-literal-canonicality | SURVIVED |\n113: \n114: 44 mutants: 29 killed, 15 survived. Every run: one named test, foreground, restored from the reviewer backup, `cmp` 0 and `git diff --quiet HEAD -- <path>` 0.\n115: \n116: ## Required before merge\n117: \n118: 1. Fix rows_test.cljc:238 (single-key assocs) and re-run the Dart lane; the three-host gate is otherwise within reach (frame-test is fully green on Dart; the other 11 rows tests pass on Dart).\n119: 2. Turn the two host exceptions in `decode` into refusals (findings 2, 3).\n120: 3. Make item 10's permutation test actually permute (finding 4) and pin at least one root id plus a non-automorphic search fixture (finding 5).\n121: 4. Decide the marker representation (finding 6); record the census-ordering reading (finding 8).\n122: The remaining low items and the surviving-mutant assertions (finding 12) can land with the same follow-up.\n123: \n124: VERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED"}],"deferred":false}}
